Original commit body from 337e4a43bbe8fa28e16dbdceea98ca572277cb0c:

The ADR-0017 taint walk consumed `django_orm_dispatch`'s `dispatches_to` edge —
class → the model's ORM methods — as if it carried a value, yielding
`function --instantiates--> Class --dispatches_to--> Class.save`, which lands on
whatever ORM method the linker attached to the class, including one the function
never calls. A `dispatches_to` edge whose SOURCE node is a type is now
reachability, not dataflow.

NOT A REVERT OF INV-zuhig, which is satisfied at P1 and put the edge type in the
walk deliberately — without it no framework-dispatched handler could mint and 18
self-proof confirms were vacuous. The cases differ structurally:
`argparse_dispatch` emits from the enclosing FUNCTION of a
`set_defaults(func=cmd_x)` registration to a handler genuinely invoked with the
data; `django_orm_dispatch` emits from a CLASS. A type node holds no value; an
instance does.

THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE SOURCE NODE'S KIND, NOT THE EMITTING LINKER. Five
linkers emit class-sourced dispatch, but two that look class-shaped are not:
`di_resolution` emits from an interface METHOD and `type_hierarchy` from a parent
METHOD, both ordinary virtual dispatch. A linker-name blocklist would have taken
those with it. The vocabulary is `type_like_kind_names()`, whose docstring
records audit 0018 finding 26 hand-written copies of that set across 24
vocabularies, five omitting `protocol`.

FAILS OPEN: an id that does not parse against ADR-0036's span anchor keeps its
old meaning. The edges are NOT deleted — they are correct as reachability, and
`django_orm_dispatch` calls that an orthogonal concern; removing them would file
the defect in the wrong artifact.

MEASUREMENT 0020, and the first result is that the FIRST DESIGN MEASURED AN
EMPTY POPULATION. On the shipped tree the fix is INERT (0 moved, 0 class hops)
because the defect needs a sink INSIDE a model method and WI-sihoh's rule was
withheld. The pre-registration predicted a decrease on a population INV-putug's
own text describes as absent; that is recorded as the design error it was.

Harness arms restore the population by pinning `py.py` to `359880a105` in BOTH
arms (common-mode, NOT shipped). Arm X reproduces 0016 round 1 exactly — 184
flows, 33 class-node hops.

  pretix  183 -> 163 situations, 22 removed / 2 added, net -20
  hops    33 -> 0
  kserve  62 -> 62, control unmoved

Net -20 matches 0016's independent attribution of 20 situations to this shape.

R1 DOES NOT FIRE, checked three ways. All 22 removals crossed a class node (zero
collateral); no source function's body calls the named sink at all; and the two
sites read at source are a no-argument `InvoiceAddress()` never saved and a
`SubEventItem.delete` never called.

THE INFORMATIVE HALF IS WHAT SURVIVED: 11 of the 33 class-hop flows were KEPT,
because `generate_invoice` really does take the tainted order and reach
`Invoice.save` through the annotated `build_invoice`. The fix deletes the
dishonest path to a finding, not the finding. 22 + 11 = 33.

